nvmet-tcp: pass iov_len instead of sg->length to bvec_set_page()

jira KERNEL-1630
cve CVE-2026-64534
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.166.1.el8_10
commit-author Varun Prakash <varun@chelsio.com>
commit 1f0bbf28940cf5edad90ab57b62aa8197bf5e836
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.166.1.el8_10/1f0bbf28.failed

iov_len is the valid data length, so pass iov_len instead of sg->length to
bvec_set_page().

Fixes: 5bfaba275ae6 ("nvmet-tcp: don't map pages which can't come from HIGHMEM")
	Signed-off-by: Rakshana Sridhar <rakshanas@chelsio.com>
	Signed-off-by: Varun Prakash <varun@chelsio.com>
	Reviewed-by: Sagi Grimberg <sagi@grimberg.me>
	Reviewed-by: Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>
	Signed-off-by: Keith Busch <kbusch@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 1f0bbf28940cf5edad90ab57b62aa8197bf5e836)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	drivers/nvme/target/tcp.c
diff --cc drivers/nvme/target/tcp.c
index f98fcd07dd20,cd92d7ddf5ed..000000000000
--- a/drivers/nvme/target/tcp.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/target/tcp.c
@@@ -323,9 -348,8 +323,14 @@@ static void nvmet_tcp_build_pdu_iovec(s
  	while (length) {
  		u32 iov_len = min_t(u32, length, sg->length - sg_offset);
  
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +		iov->bv_page = sg_page(sg);
 +		iov->bv_len = sg->length;
 +		iov->bv_offset = sg->offset + sg_offset;
++=======
+ 		bvec_set_page(iov, sg_page(sg), iov_len,
+ 				sg->offset + sg_offset);
++>>>>>>> 1f0bbf28940c (nvmet-tcp: pass iov_len instead of sg->length to bvec_set_page())
  
  		length -= iov_len;
  		sg = sg_next(sg);
* Unmerged path drivers/nvme/target/tcp.c
